[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Buff" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" uid="uid://cqrqkdgcf8mti" path="res://engine/character/buff/buff.gd" id="1_buff"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_buff")
; A PURE MARKER: action_eyes_of_night.gd reads it through UnitCondition.has_buff and nothing else
; reads it at all. buff_mark_of_the_dead.tres is the same file with a different clock.
;
; until = 1 is Lancer.UNTIL.END_OF_NEXT_TURN (lancer.gd:48). turn_count ticks at the WEARER's turn
; start (unit_condition.gd:24) and end_turn_for_statuses clears once it reads 1 (:40-41): pressed
; mid-turn at count 0, it survives this turn's end, the enemy's whole turn, the Sluagh's next turn
; start, and clears at THAT turn's end. "Until the end of your next turn."
until = 1
; VISIBLE, per ruling 22 - it is the only thing on the board that says the Gate is open. Its `icon`
; is SP5's, which is why test_every_visible_buff_has_a_real_icon carries one more failing assert
; from this task on.
;
; IT WRITES NO ROWS OF ITS OWN, ON PURPOSE, AND THAT IS PINNED (final review, item 1). Translate.buff
; falls through to the OWNER GEAR's actions[0] when a buff has no rows of its own (translate.gd:72-77)
; - and on THIS Kit actions[0] IS the activate, so the chip renders "Activate Bleakshadow Gate" /
; "Until the end of your next turn, you gain the EYES OF NIGHT reaction", which is exactly what the
; chip means: the Gate is open. Nothing is invented and nothing is borrowed wrongly.
;
; THE MEMORY RULE (lancer-tactics-buff-card-fallback) SAYS A MULTI-ACTION KIT'S CHIP MUST NOT BORROW
; BY ACCIDENT - the fallback SUCCEEDS whatever it lands on, so no resolution guard ever fires and a
; wrong card is silent. This Kit HAS two actions (the activate and EYES OF NIGHT), which is precisely
; the shape the rule warns about; it is safe here only because the reaction is actions[1]. Reorder
; the actions array and this chip starts reading the reaction's trigger text at a unit that has not
; reacted. test_bleakshadow_gate.test_the_gate_chip_borrows_the_activates_card_on_purpose is the
; guard: it asserts the chip's own rows are ABSENT from the compiled translation AND that
; name_text()/effect_text() equal the activate's rows, so either half of the arrangement changing
; goes red. buff_wicked_host is this mod's precedent for a deliberately row-less chip.
